title: Cell Biology
subject: Biology
level: GCSE
emoji: 🔬
description: Cell structure, microscopy, transport and cell division.
---
What is the function of the nucleus? :: Contains DNA/genetic material and controls the activities of the cell.
What is the function of mitochondria? :: Site of aerobic respiration, releasing energy for the cell.
What is the function of ribosomes? :: Site of protein synthesis.
What does the cell membrane do? :: Controls which substances enter and leave the cell.
Which organelles are found in plant cells but NOT animal cells? :: Cell wall, permanent vacuole and chloroplasts.
What is the cell wall of a plant made from? :: Cellulose, which strengthens the cell.
What is the function of chloroplasts? :: Contain chlorophyll and are the site of photosynthesis.
What is the cytoplasm? :: Jelly-like substance where most chemical reactions in the cell happen.
How do prokaryotic cells differ from eukaryotic cells? :: Prokaryotes have no nucleus; their DNA is a single loop in the cytoplasm.
Give an example of a prokaryote. :: Bacteria.
What is diffusion? :: Net movement of particles from a region of higher concentration to a region of lower concentration.
What is osmosis? :: Diffusion of water across a partially permeable membrane from a dilute solution to a more concentrated solution.
What is active transport? :: Movement of substances from a low to a high concentration against the gradient, using energy from respiration.
Magnification formula? :: Magnification = image size ÷ real size.
What is a stem cell? :: An undifferentiated cell that can divide and differentiate into specialised cell types.
What is differentiation? :: The process by which a cell becomes specialised for its job.
What happens in mitosis? :: A cell divides to produce two genetically identical diploid daughter cells (used for growth and repair).
What is the cell cycle? :: A series of stages: DNA replication, mitosis, then cytokinesis (cell splits in two).
Which type of microscope has higher magnification and resolution: light or electron? :: Electron microscope.
What is meiosis? :: Cell division producing four genetically different haploid gametes.
Name two adaptations of a root hair cell. :: Long thin extension giving a large surface area; many mitochondria for active transport.
